+ *   - AS_TRANSTAB carries flags, not just an address: ADRMODE_TABLE (0b11)
+ *     in bits 1..0 and READ_INNER (bit 2), and SHARE_OUTER (bit 4) when
+ *     walks are coherent -- here they are not.
+ *   - AS_TRANSCFG is ADRMODE_LEGACY, zero: no INA_BITS.
+ *   - AS_MEMATTR is index 0 = 0x88 (implementation defined), 1 = 0x8d
+ *     (write allocate), 2 = 0x88.
+ *   - A leaf is type 0b01 (BLOCK) even at the last level, not 0b11, and
+ *     the permissions are stage-2-like: bits 7..6 are HAP, 0b11 for read
+ *     and write.  No access flag is set.
+ *   - Tables are type 0b11 at every level but the last.
+ *
+ * The A10's MMU reports 48 virtual bits and 40 physical (MMU_FEATURES
+ * 0x2830: VA_BITS = 0x30, PA_BITS = 0x28), and Panfrost gives Mali a full
+ * four-level table regardless, so the indices are bits 47..39, 38..30,
+ * 29..21 and 20..12.
+ *
+ * Probe79 runs the job through that shape first.  It then keeps the two
+ * ARMv8 shapes probe78 tried (ADRMODE 6 with INA_BITS 55 - 48, leaf type
+ * 0b11, AP stage-1 style) as fallbacks, so one boot still answers whether
+ * this GPU prefers Panfrost's format or the architectural one.
